WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.129 --> 00:00:01.789
- I wish that Starbucks had like,

00:00:01.789 --> 00:00:03.785
the for dummies menu,
where it actually tells

00:00:03.785 --> 00:00:05.989
you what all these drink names mean.

00:00:09.647 --> 00:00:11.564
- [Voiceover] I've tried
coffee, but never Starbucks.

00:00:11.564 --> 00:00:12.561
- I don't like coffee.

00:00:12.561 --> 00:00:13.862
- I've been in a Starbucks if that counts.

00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:15.870
- If I put a ton of milk
in it, it'll be okay.

00:00:17.602 --> 00:00:19.809
- Standard Starbucks coffee.

00:00:19.809 --> 00:00:20.749
- It smells terrible.

00:00:20.749 --> 00:00:22.328
- I usually like the smell of coffee,

00:00:22.328 --> 00:00:24.047
this one does seem really bitter to me.

00:00:24.047 --> 00:00:25.832
- Alright, here I go.

00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:33.647
- It's smooth, I'll give it that.

00:00:33.647 --> 00:00:34.920
- Nothing special about it.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.748
Not for me anyway.

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:36.515
- Burnt dirt.

00:00:36.515 --> 00:00:37.981
- I don't know how people drink this.

00:00:37.981 --> 00:00:39.617
- Tastes a little bit
more like machine oil

00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:40.819
than it does coffee.

00:00:43.259 --> 00:00:44.234
- So this looks fun.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.483
- Real coffee drinkers think
this is basically dessert.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.133
- Is there coffee in this?

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:51.459
- That's not bad.

00:00:51.459 --> 00:00:52.154
- I get it now.

00:00:52.154 --> 00:00:53.558
- It's like a milkshake,
with just a little

00:00:53.558 --> 00:00:55.253
bit of coffee flavor.

00:00:55.253 --> 00:00:56.600
- It's just sugar.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.913
- This is probably what God enjoys every

00:00:57.913 --> 00:00:58.714
single morning.

00:00:58.714 --> 00:00:59.839
- Yeah, the only reason that I like this

00:00:59.839 --> 00:01:01.297
is because it's barely coffee.

00:01:01.297 --> 00:01:03.666
Which I imagine is the
reason why it's so popular.

00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:05.558
- I could see people
like, associating a drink

00:01:05.558 --> 00:01:07.799
like this with the "basic" term.

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:09.343
- People be like, "Mmm, drinking coffee",

00:01:09.343 --> 00:01:10.725
but you're not drinking coffee.

00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:12.222
- But those basic bitches are clearly

00:01:12.222 --> 00:01:13.197
on to something.

00:01:13.197 --> 00:01:13.860
- Can I keep this?

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:14.533
- [Woman] Yeah.

00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:15.588
- Excellent.

00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:18.770
- [Brown Hair Girl] It sounds like,

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.530
very foreign and exciting
like, "Oh, I'll have

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.306
"a caramel macchiato."

00:01:22.306 --> 00:01:23.814
- Wasn't it started in Seattle?

00:01:23.814 --> 00:01:26.485
Like, let's drop this Italian pretense.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:27.253
- Nope.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.796
- This I actually...

00:01:28.796 --> 00:01:29.793
Don't mind.

00:01:29.793 --> 00:01:31.675
- This is more of an adult drink.

00:01:31.675 --> 00:01:33.671
- Would totally rather
have the frappuccino

00:01:33.671 --> 00:01:35.061
than the macchiato.

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.895
- This is for indecisive people.

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:39.643
People who are like, "I don't wanna drink

00:01:39.643 --> 00:01:41.942
"straight up coffee,
but I also don't wanna

00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:44.403
"have the guilt that comes
along with this one."

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.830
- If it was a matter of life and death,

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.162
and I had to pick a coffee
item from Starbucks,

00:01:49.162 --> 00:01:51.565
I would pick the caramel macchiato.

00:01:51.565 --> 00:01:52.976
Life or death though.

00:01:53.952 --> 00:01:55.311
- Oh, I don't think
they live up to the hype

00:01:55.311 --> 00:01:55.869
at all.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:57.053
- I'll definitely go back
for that frappuccino.

00:01:57.053 --> 00:01:58.713
- I'm not going to start drinking coffee.

00:01:58.713 --> 00:02:00.408
- If I did go to Starbucks
again, I would just

00:02:00.408 --> 00:02:01.650
order these.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.786
- I don't think that their
product is necessarily

00:02:03.786 --> 00:02:05.771
superior to anyone else's.

00:02:05.771 --> 00:02:08.289
- I'm gonna turn into Bevis at any moment.

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:10.890
Cappuccino!

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.026
Macchiato for my bung hole!

